hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"332","Narrated by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Alaa. Narrated by Sufyan. He said: We preserved it from al-Zuhri. He said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha. H. Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Dhabi and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Makhzoumi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was rising in my room. The Fay will appear yet,” Ahmed said: “In her room.” Abu Bakr said: Appearance among the Arabs has two meanings: one is for something to appear so that it can be seen and become clear, so there is nothing hidden, and the second is that A thing prevails over another thing, as the Arabs say: So-and-so defeated so-and-so, and so-and-so’s army defeated so-and-so’s army, that is, he defeated them, so the meaning of her saying is: He did not The fa’ has not yet appeared, i.e. the fa’ has not overcome the sun in its room, i.e. the shadow in the room was not greater than the sun during the afternoon prayer."
